      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Check each parameter size before copying it to CPU in `UVAOffloader`.\n- Stop before a parameter would push the cumulative logical payload beyond\n  `--cpu-offload-gb`.\n- Count the precomputed parameter payload size after a successful offload.\n\nThis enforces the configured logical CPU offload budget at parameter admission\ntime. It does not claim that RSS or allocator-backed host memory is an exact\nmatch for the configured value.\n\n## Why this is not duplicate work\n\nThe open [#56413](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/56413) avoids\nduplicate host allocation in the UVA path and retains pinning for the non-UVA\nfallback. It addresses physical host allocation behavior, but does not prevent\na whole parameter from pushing the cumulative logical payload past the\nconfigured budget.\n\nThe open [#54610](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54610) prioritizes\nsparse MoE parameters and preserves lazy layer construction. Its offload loop\nstill checks only whether the current total has reached the limit before\noffloading the next whole parameter. Its discussion reports 47.69 GB of\ntracked offload with `--cpu-offload-gb 47`, which is the over-admission guarded\nby this PR.\n\nThe merged [#57834](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57834) releases\nthe process-global offloader during shutdown and does not overlap with this\nbudget check.\n\n## Validation\n\n- End-to-end regression test\n  `tests/basic_correctness/cpu_offload/test_cpu_offload.py::test_cpu_offload_respects_byte_budget`: 1 passed. It loads\n  `hmellor/tiny-random-LlamaForCausalLM` through `vllm_runner` with a 1-byte\n  CPU offload budget and verifies that the tracked logical bytes never exceed\n  the configured maximum.\n- `tests/model_executor/offloader/test_prefetch.py`: 6 passed.\n- Ruff check, format check, and pre-commit hooks: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nNo model evaluation was run because this only changes offload admission and\ndoes not change model computation or output semantics.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nAI assistance was used to inspect the repository, verify duplicate work,\nimplement the fix and regression test, and run the validation above. The human\nsubmitter must review and understand every changed line before responding to\nreview.\n",
